            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elizabeth Duckworth"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is perfect if ........A). you don't know how to cook, B). your imagination has dried up, C). your camping, D). you have a really fresh (freshly caught) piece of salmon and you don't want to adulterate it with any diverting seasonings. In my past, I have utilized all categories A to D.\nI did pan fry my salmon two nights ago, I used salt and pepper, two tablespoons unsalted butter and a splash of sesame oil to the burning (smoking). Served with a rice pilaf, a green salad with a vinaigrette dressing. With a cold crisp white sauvignon, it's a meal to serve a queen!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lisa meehan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a little garlic powder and pepper with the sea salt and took the advice on a comment to cut down the time frying on the flesh side (fried about 2-3min instead). It turned out great and I have a 19 month d and a 4yr old who agreed!\nServed with asparagus and garlic \nshell noodles.",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-11T02:51:29.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melody"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Only thing I did differently is I covered the skillet while the salmon cooked, it does not dry out this way in my opinion! Great easy and quick recipe. Thank you!!",
            "datePublished": "2022-01-05T18:32:27.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Wicksy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my favourite way to cook salmon! I use rice bran oil (it tolerates higher heat than olive oil) and a little butter. Altho I sort of do it the opposite...cook skin side down for about 7 min. then turn it just to brown the top. Then you don't have to mess around taking the skin off to make \"crackle\". The crackle is delish!",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-22T02:56:18.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Malice"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like the reviewer said, this is PERFECT to those who are new and fresh to cooking. The great aspect about this recipe is that it teaches to how to cook salmon, and only mentions the bare ingredients you CAN NOT go without to achieve that. Is you are like me and like some more flavor, go with this: saute onions w/ garlic in the pan before adding the salmon and then last, after the salmon is added, place some freshly cut tomatoes within the same pan. This will add a LOAD of extra flavor for a family favorite. :)",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-18T13:26:17.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mom of 3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just made this for my husband. He doesn’t like added salt so just pepper. I also cooked it a bit less because he had a thinner piece with no skin. I made it into a sandwich with a mayonnaise recipe I found here (Valerie’s sauce), lettuce and tomato on wheat toast. He was raving!",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-01T01:14:20.977Z"
          },
          {
